:question/math-academy-id "q-137883" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $W,$ and the vector $b$ above. If the normal equation for the corresponding weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 36 \\\\ 36 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {1}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 16 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}72 & 36 \\\\ 36 & 18\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=72+18+18=108.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-137883/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af51b0b6-4ae7-5b6a-b151-7f8cb88fa186"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-137883"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-137880/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "fc96f3d8-ff04-5328-b105-9a21f3b34b4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137880/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "116bffe7-c1c0-58f6-9dbf-a91427f80f72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137880/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "ee97f753-ec6e-5f44-8323-f313b3a46145" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137880/selection/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" :answer/id #uuid "96c33eff-4bd1-568e-904c-8db603fd63fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137880/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "d9f03312-f6e7-5c85-8250-4b6d2a5d95dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137880/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbe850bc-f01c-5be8-9f61-d137407be077" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-137880/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-137880/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-137880/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060