{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 & 27 \\\\ -4 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}17 & 23 \\\\ 23 & 85\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 23\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=17+85+13=115.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-137881/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af51b0b6-4ae7-5b6a-b151-7f8cb88fa186"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-137881"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-137887/selection/362d6474c6f01bbd84dd4aad1f36df5c29d2ebafec9135e07e89e7292a2cd334" :answer/id #uuid "00cc5b21-c378-5ecb-a645-67ca3699e75f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "101" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137887/selection/4dfff855611bc1c5fe6586768d23b9310d2c2cf22a055d87028e97c636d2fd64" :answer/id #uuid "dd97dabe-55e4-5bbe-bcd4-7aaadaa01a3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "116" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137887/s