begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {1}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {1}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-8 & 12 \\\\ 4 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 12 & -6 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}36 & -42 \\\\ -42 & 81\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=36+81+(-16)=101.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-137887/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "af51b0b6-4ae7-5b6a-b151-7f8cb88fa186"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-137887"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158458/selection/c5b1c452fbbf695d51774e4fdb54a1ea7a83bfb5edb76e399d7d1b89ecc5113e" :answer/id #uuid "64a6ff10-e7a4-507f-a9df-4ee39807b5f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158458/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "507f5ccf-4321-5935-ae66-3b892d009ee7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158458/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "9a4d6170-41ac-538b-8188-2fa95298174f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158458/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "fc66ab9c-d132-5548-a7cf-de1a64f42d19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158458/selection/4d9c42c5d00c4f8dc12f95d2b791d1f64193f69dbf1a785f2edc40bbc9c10ef0" :answer/id #uuid "bd6f405f-cb4d-5c0d-8947-7ef1d2ffdbb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158458/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "80a7380a-da90-5a63-a74d-ec4e0506623f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158458/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-158458/selection/c5b1c452fbbf695d51774e4fdb54a1ea7a83bfb5edb76e399d7d1b89ecc5113e" "q-158458/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-158458/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-158458/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-158458/selection/4d9c42c5d00c4f8dc12f95d2b791d1f64193f69dbf1a785f2edc40bbc9c10ef0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158458" :question/id #uuid "21cfa25d-c89a-5529-8457-337b4bbfd898" :question/math-academy-id "q-158458" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $W,$ and the vector $b$ shown above. If the general solution for the weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb$ is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of  $17a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {1}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -4 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}17 & -34 \\\\ -34 & 68\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the above matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}17 & -34 & 3 \\\\ -34 & 68 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}17 & -34 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{3}{17}+2{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{17}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{17} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n17a+\\frac{b}{c}=17(\\frac{3}{17})+\\frac{2}{1}=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-158458/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b21c27bd-5c7a-5645-93b5-0af73c59f685"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158458"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-137926/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "a8827e45-e55e-5d34-b841-1e4ac6f01cac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137926/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "39a46557-f844-5328-a540-4100c85efbe3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137926/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "10ebfe21-1cc3-59cb-b3a5-7e1e26d780b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137926/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "8a167df7-5cfe-5995-91b8-395e3197eb5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137926/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "bd6811c6-74ef-5ae4-a242-24a9217093a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137926/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6b34610-7c67-572d-a238-284fca12821a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-137926/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-137926/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-137926/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-137926/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-137926/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-137926/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-137926" :question/id #uuid "687aaec7-7707-5832-95a4-45283b14d78f" :question/math-academy-id "q-137926" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $W,$ and the vector $b$ shown above. If the general solution for the weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb$ is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of  $a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {3}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 & 18 \\\\ -8 & -16 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 36\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}25 & 50 \\\\ 50 & 100\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}50 \\\\ 100\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the above matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}25 & 50 & 50 \\\\ 50 & 100 & 100\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}25 & 50 & 50 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=2-2{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+\\frac{b}{c}=2+\\frac{(-2)}{1}=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-137926/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b21c27bd-5c7a-5645-93b5-0af73c59f685"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-137926"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158372/selection/c8239dbe3e50a76e325cbfa353dfa6a4dd6a8b07d222daebe023ba45343e253d" :answer/id #uuid "52f97b4b-25f4-5f23-9d37-ebbd3437a400" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158372/selection/60eadf18022e36714cee17e0479ab6af66a6361ceef7571ec8305b4e57ee6d8f" :answer/id #uuid "2764f830-4551-56c9-86fc-b43051419c98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158372/selection/a64189931ea8bea8b327ff02de88f18f3275caec4f7a980dc17103f5c1bc31fb" :answer/id #uuid "5dc589de-7dec-5fbe-883a-0790141cf88c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158372/selection/89a7b50043145b047ec0b49f3140fd1e1b3e4de0bc9d81a9f50ac0b4c1e9f136" :answer/id #uuid "2e69bb92-2b1f-5b60-8f67-1168e8cd4c4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158372/selection/80f7643749639dc6ac3cb6ea590a80572731108334d6c4e6c17a301b44d6338a" :answer/id #uuid "b6e8ca4c-99e8-5a4e-bbda-510188ad6079" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158372/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1fa9091-24c3-576e-b9b6-9246976a502d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158372/selection/89a7b50043145b047ec0b49f3140fd1e1b3e4de0bc9d81a9f50ac0b4c1e9f136" :answer-field/choices ["q-158372/selection/c8239dbe3e50a76e325cbfa353dfa6a4dd6a8b07d222daebe023ba45343e253d" "q-158372/selection/60eadf18022e36714cee17e0479ab6af66a6361ceef7571ec8305b4e57ee6d8f" "q-158372/selection/a64189931ea8bea8b327ff02de88f18f3275caec4f7a980dc17103f5c1bc31fb" "q-158372/selection/89a7b50043145b047ec0b49f3140fd1e1b3e4de0bc9d81a9f50ac0b4c1e9f136" "q-158372/selection/80f7643749639dc6ac3cb6ea590a80572731108334d6c4e6c17a301b44d6338a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158372" :question/id #uuid "ed199a9d-a3a2-5954-968b-924b5a1b21d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-158372" :question/problem "Find the solution for the weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {1}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}14 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the matrix on the left-hand side is invertible, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & ={[\\begin{aligned}14 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{14\\cdot 9-9\\cdot 9}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -9 \\\\ -9 & 14\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{45}[\\begin{aligned}45 \\\\ -45\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-158372/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b21c27bd-5c7a-5645-93b5-0af73c59f685"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158372"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-137917/selection/80f7643749639dc6ac3cb6ea590a80572731108334d6c4e6c17a301b44d6338a" :answer/id #uuid "28949789-16b1-54dd-a2d4-92dc4fb8d31a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137917/selection/89509341da3fc059d3fae3c08ea87f7c7273dd2cfed4f405dd9f061ed448811c" :answer/id #uuid "c0c45a8b-cf01-5874-9937-5e921c8d910c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137917/selection/dd384871c0bc1fca475e51fa9975b2c7867938d8313eef675c9512786643a778" :answer/id #uuid "dd1b2f9b-da35-5493-a1c3-bcafcdfe9139" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137917/selection/4afe72ce1ff2948bb282f72a051259b7c7c995391c6a8ae0e3d05b32a2584b91" :answer/id #uuid "70e98e58-f2b4-5eed-aa29-77bcc06cd1da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137917/selection/fa3f23c7334055936c2275cd39a879c618af1144bc7e7a75445f0ec46dcc7115" :answer/id #uuid "db24d403-8550-5e1d-bf39-94857849b2ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137917/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc070760-aaa1-5820-b759-73b0f77fb4c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-137917/selection/fa3f23c7334055936c2275cd39a879c618af1144bc7e7a75445f0ec46dcc7115" :answer-field/choices ["q-137917/selection/80f7643749639dc6ac3cb6ea590a80572731108334d6c4e6c17a301b44d6338a" "q-137917/selection/89509341da3fc059d3fae3c08ea87f7c7273dd2cfed4f405dd9f061ed448811c" "q-137917/selection/dd384871c0bc1fca475e51fa9975b2c7867938d8313eef675c9512786643a778" "q-137917/selection/4afe72ce1ff2948bb282f72a051259b7c7c995391c6a8ae0e3d05b32a2584b91" "q-137917/selection/fa3f23c7334055936c2275cd39a879c618af1144bc7e7a75445f0ec46dcc7115"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-137917" :question/id #uuid "d5e94b33-5b31-5ebd-87d2-7bfed384ef0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-137917" :question/problem "Find the solution for the weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {1}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {1}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the matrix on the left-hand side is invertible, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-137917/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b21c27bd-5c7a-5645-93b5-0af73c59f685"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-137917"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-137920/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "0282c921-d961-5223-b42b-e7a7bcdb6b02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-137920/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "4af57463-cfd2-536d-aa19-114cc42d71fb" :answer/type :answer.type